Repro (post-fix, tip commit 97bceb4ac): UserApp GlobalSearchScreen (module-selection
landing -> "Search all categories" -> query "Cheeseburger"), item_id=553 @ Noodle Bar
(Abu Dhabi zone, zone_id=2 -- NOTE: ticket text says "zone1 Demo Zone Dhaka", but the
DB shows Noodle Bar/item 553 is actually zone_id=2/Abu Dhabi; flagged as drift).
Logged in customer@nears.com. Item added to cart via the card-level quick "+" button
(CartCountView) WITHOUT ever entering any module -- ModuleController.module stays null
AND the identity-scoped SharedPreferences cache key `cacheModuleId::u:<number>` was
NEVER WRITTEN this session (verified via `run-as ... cat FlutterSharedPreferences.xml`
-- no module-related key present at all, confirmed by grep). This is the exact
repro state the ticket's own AC/QA-scope describes: "GLOBAL/cross-module search path
... so that ModuleController.module is null when quick-remove is tapped".

Tapping the same card's quick "Remove" control (qty stepper, qty=1) still 400s:

