App DID emit a paired AppLogger.failure [FAIL] line (AC4 -- confirmed NOT regressed).

ROOT CAUSE OF THE FIX GAP: cart_repository.dart's new `_resolveFreshCacheModuleId()`
(the NEARS-2753 fix) only helps when the SharedPreferences module cache is STALE
(present but from a prior identity/module) -- the exact NEARS-2490 scenario it mirrors.
It does NOT help when the cache was NEVER WRITTEN in the first place, i.e. the user
never entered ANY module this session before adding to cart purely via the global
search quick-add button (which bypasses GlobalSearchController.ensureModuleContext
entirely -- that guard only runs on the card-level tap / "See all", not on the
CartCountView's own add/remove InkWells). In that state BOTH ModuleController.module
AND the cached-module SharedPreferences key are null, so `header` still omits
AppConstants.moduleId, and the DELETE 400s exactly as before the fix.

AC3 -- the raw backend string IS still shown to the user. Caught via a tight
uiautomator-dump poll (0.3s interval) immediately after the tap:
  content-desc="Module id required"
(archived: bug-raw-error-toast-dump.xml). This is `ApiChecker.checkApi`'s existing,
UNCHANGED `showCustomSnackBar(response.statusText, ...)` call -- statusText is set
from the backend's `{message: ...}` envelope in `ApiClient.handleResponse`, so any
400 with this shape is toasted verbatim regardless of this fix.

SEPARATE, PRE-EXISTING (NOT part of this diff) UI-desync note: `CartController
.removeFromCart` synchronously does `_cartList.removeAt(index)` then a BARE
`update()` (no ids). `CartCountView`'s `GetBuilder<CartController>` is registered
with `id: CartController.cartBadgeId(item.id)` (verified against get-4.7.3 source:
`GetBuilder(id: ...)` registers via `addListenerId` into `_updatersGroupIds`, which
`refresh()`/bare `update()` never iterates -- only `_updaters`, the id-less list).
So the search-results item card's own stepper NEVER visually reflects a remove
(qty stays "1" onscreen) even though `_cartList` truly drops the row locally --
regardless of whether the server DELETE succeeds. Confirmed live: after the FIRST
"Remove" tap, `_cartList` no longer contains this row (later "Remove" taps produce
NO new network calls at all -- `optimisticStep`'s `_localIndexOf` returns -1 and
the decrement branch no-ops), yet the card visibly still shows qty "1" the whole
time. This means AC1 ("item removed ... row gone") cannot be visually demonstrated
on this screen at all -- a second, independent defect compounding the 400. Flagged
as a regression-candidate (pre-existing, not touched by this diff) rather than a
task_bug of this ticket, since `removeFromCart`'s bare `update()` line is unchanged
by commit 97bceb4ac.
